After being laughed at by my friends for all the annoying ways I died
("You feel here a cockatrice corpse..."), I finally managed to ascend. The RNG
gave me a dwarvish valkyrie, who swiftly made her way to the oracle. A killer
bee showed her that the amulet she wore was Versus Poison. Ever since I had a
valkyrie with only 4 str under her GoP, I wait with the mines until I have
poison resistance. The watch captian had fallen through a hole, so it was easy
to let Touchwood survive there. I found a polymorph trap at the bottom of the
mines. Sator became a red dragon, Touchwood a silver one. After a bit of
protection, I let them eat the cross-aligned priest and converted the Minetown
altar. Dipping for Excalibur, I accidently released a water demon, who gave me
SDSM. The lady of the lake seemed to have a day off, so I decided to skip
Excalibur and go straight for Mjollnir, which was just a few sacrifices away.
A few more sacrifices gave me Sunsword as a permanent light source.

Touchwood or Sator accidently killed the oracle, Sokoban gave a bag of holding.
A throne on level 10 gave me the cloak of magic resistance, while a chest
somewhere around here contained a "oLS.  The Quest was easy, but very rewarding,
because there was a /oWishing just outside Lord Surturs lair. 

Medusa was a bit of a problem, because I still hadn't found something to
levitate with, so I took a dive through a trap door. Coming up again, I did what
I always did: I took my pets with me. "Sator turns to stone!". Perseus did not
have the boots of levitation, so I ended up wishing for a ring.

A first round of alchemy gave me ~400 HP, so Gehennom was easy. With an AC of
-25, nothing came even close to stopping me. I found another "oLS and boots of
speed, simply lying on the dungeon floor. Another round of alchemy and
scrollwriting gave me ~500 HP, AC -40.

The wizard never gave me any troubles. The first few times I shot him with a
/oDeath, but as I wanted to save some charges for the riders, I've also defeated
him in hand to hand combat. 

The sanctum was a piece of cake. A nalfeshnee summoned Yeenoghu, who took the
amulet for me.

The elemental planes were also easy. A ring of conflict works wonders. It is a
bit annoying on the plane of fire though, with all the fire elementals needing
to show they're unhurt.

On the Astral plane, Pestilence gave a bit of a problem, because my wand refused
to hit him. I ended up wishing for another one. Luckily, I had taken the right
altar, so my first ascension was a fact.

Next one is going to be some non-fighter. Too bad there isn't a limited random
option, so you can have the RNG choose between for instance, only a wizard, a
monk and a tourist.

